1. void foo(unsigned char u8a, unsigned char u16a)
2. {
3.  u8a = (unsigned char)(u8a << 8);
4.  u16a = (unsigned short)((unsigned short)u8a << 9);
5. }
Line 3: An unsigned char type value is shifted by 8 bits. Because size of unsigned char is 8 bits, this shift is larger than the size.

input.dangerousExampleKo:
1. void foo(unsigned char u8a, unsigned char u16a)
2. {
3.  u8a = (unsigned char)(u8a << 8);
4.  u16a = (unsigned short)((unsigned short)u8a << 9);
5. }
라인 3: unsigned char 타입의 값을 8비트 만큼 시프트합니다. unsigned char는 8비트 밖에 표현하지 못하기 때문에 표현 한계를 넘어가게 됩니다.

